== a gate that opens by itself (kardinal why demo prod)
prod is held by gate no-weekend-deploys.
  Version  1.5.0 (demo-b)
  Why      Production deployments are blocked on weekends
  Rule     !schedule.isWeekend
  Now      !schedule.isWeekend = false
  Opens    by itself when the expression passes; rechecked every 5m
  Next     wait: it opens by itself when the expression passes (kardinal status demo -w follows it)
  Or       kardinal override demo prod --gate no-weekend-deploys --reason <why>

== a soak gate: how far it soaked and when it opens (kardinal why demo prod)
prod is held by gate uat-soak.
  Version  1.5.0 (demo-b)
  Why      A version must run in uat for 3 minutes before prod
  Rule     bundle.upstreamSoakMinutes >= 3
  Now      soak 0.4 of 3 min in uat
  Opens    by itself in about 2m36s; rechecked every 30s
  Next     wait: it opens by itself in about 2m36s (kardinal status demo -w follows it)
  Or       kardinal override demo prod --gate uat-soak --reason <why>

== a soak gate before its upstream is live (kardinal why demo prod)
prod is held by gate uat-soak.
  Version  1.5.0 (demo-b)
  Rule     upstream.uat.soakMinutes > 9
  Now      uat not live yet, needs 10 min of soak
  Opens    by itself 10 min after uat is live; rechecked every 5m
  Next     wait: it opens by itself 10 min after uat is live (kardinal status demo -w follows it)
  Or       kardinal override demo prod --gate uat-soak --reason <why>

